  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image-only, singleprofile, resnet50) achieves only 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality with a large gap. The key uncertainty now is whether the profile setting (single vs. multi) and aggregation strategy can improve RNA performance, which is the foundational design choice for all subsequent multimodal experiments. This experiment (config_002: RNA-only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) directly tests whether aggregating multiple cell profiles via average pooling improves over the single-profile baseline, while holding the encoder constant. It is the minimal, cleanest extension of config_001, isolating the multiprofile+aggregation variable. If it helps, it validates the multiprofile direction and informs all multimodal configs; if it does not, it prunes a large portion of the search space (all multiprofile variants) under a limited budget. Choosing avgpool over transformer first is conservative: it tests whether any aggregation benefit exists before committing to a more complex aggregator."
}

